---
/*
 * "You are signed in. Press this to create the workspace." The step that normally does NOT
 * appear.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHY A PRESS EXISTS HERE AT ALL, WHEN THE HAPPY PATH HAS NONE
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Coming back from GitHub, the page creates the workspace by itself: the reader already
 * pressed a button that said what would happen, and making them press a second one to
 * confirm the thing they asked for is ceremony. This panel is for the two cases where
 * creating without asking would be a guess:
 *
 *   1. THE PAGE COULD NOT READ WHAT THEY ALREADY HAVE. Before creating anything unprompted
 *      the script calls myWorkspaces() to check whether this identity already owns one. If
 *      that read fails — a network blip, a schema that is not exposed — the script does not
 *      know whether creating would be their first workspace or their fourth, so it stops and
 *      asks. Creating on a failed read is how you mint a duplicate.
 *   2. THEY ASKED FOR ANOTHER ONE. "Create another workspace" from the finished panel lands
 *      here, and here they get to name it, because a second workspace called exactly what the
 *      first one is called is not a name.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THE NAME FIELD
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * maxlength is 80 and the field is required, which is not a guess: the server validates the
 * name with `boundedText(command.name, 80)` and boundedText's default minimum is 1
 * (supabase/functions/command/index.ts). Over-long or empty is a 400 the reader would have to
 * decode, so the field refuses it first. The default value is filled in by the page's script
 * from the GitHub handle on the session; it is a default, not a decision, and it is editable.
 *
 * There is no "check if this name is taken" — names are not unique in the schema and nothing
 * on the server would answer that question.
 */

import "./panel.css";
import Button from "../ui/Button.astro";
---

<section class="st-pn" data-panel="ready" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="pn-ready-t" hidden>
  <h2 class="st-pn__t" id="pn-ready-t">Name your workspace</h2>
  <p class="st-pn__p" data-ready-note>
    You are signed in. This creates one workspace on your account.
  </p>

  <label class="st-pn__field">
    <span class="st-pn__label">Workspace name</span>
    <input
      class="st-pn__input"
      data-ws-name-input
      type="text"
      name="workspace-name"
      maxlength="80"
      required
      autocomplete="off"
      spellcheck="false"
    />
  </label>

  <div class="st-pn__act">
    <Button data-create size="lg">Create workspace</Button>
  </div>

  <p class="st-pn__who">
    Signed in as <strong data-who>your GitHub account</strong>. Not you?
    <button class="st-pn__linkbtn" type="button" data-signout>Sign out</button>.
  </p>
</section>
